{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775332925-Pn8lxlgIiEURgYwGnT9C","role":"assistant","created":1775332931,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"It seems like this document only contains data from the October 1969 Treasury Bulletin. The data for January 1970, 1971, etc. should be in different issues of the Treasury Bulletin. But looking at the file structure, it appears all the data is in one large file.\n\nLet me look more carefully at what's in the file. The manifest mentions:\n- January 1970, page 32\n- January 1971, page 24\n- etc.\n\nBut all these seem to be pointing to the same source file. Let me check if the data for those years is somewhere in the text file.\n\nActually wait - looking at the JSON more carefully - let me search for elements with different page numbers and look at the content more carefully.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_05d94a67846143118fd0bf44","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport json\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1969_10.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Let's find all elements that contain table data and look at page numbers\n# Look for elements that might contain debt info for different years\n\n# Let's look at all elements that mention \"Federal debt\" \nfor i, el in enumerate(data['document']['elements']):\n    content = el.get('content', '')\n    if not content:\n        continue\n    if 'FD-1' in content or 'FD-2' in content or 'Total outstanding' in content:\n        # Get page number\n        bbox = el.get('bbox', [])\n        pages = set()\n        for b in bbox:\n            if 'page_id' in b:\n                pages.add(b['page_id'])\n        print(f\"Element {i}, pages: {pages}\")\n        print(f\"  Content preview: {content[:200]}\")\n        print()\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
